Cause: Windows OpenProcess failures were all treated as active, so ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER for a vanished PID prevented next-launch orphan cleanup forever. Fix: only that documented missing-process error is inactive; access denial and unknown failures remain fail-closed. Proof: regression test first failed to compile before the classifier existed, then passed; npm run test:installer passed with 54 Rust tests and 2 ignored plus all frontend/boundary checks; cargo clippy -D warnings passed; Windows GNU cargo check --tests passed.
